Rewrite the following Java 8 code into exactly 5 different variants. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Each variant should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input. Make the variants meaningfully different from one another and from the original code, while preserving functionality exactly.
Print all 5 rewritten variants, numbered from 1 to 5. Do not stop early, do not skip an index, and do not repeat an index. Use this exact format:
<perturbed_code_1>
<your_rewritten_code_1>
</perturbed_code_1>
<perturbed_code_2>
<your_rewritten_code_2>
</perturbed_code_2>
<perturbed_code_3>
<your_rewritten_code_3>
</perturbed_code_3>
<perturbed_code_4>
<your_rewritten_code_4>
</perturbed_code_4>
<perturbed_code_5>
<your_rewritten_code_5>
</perturbed_code_5>
Each block must contain one complete program. Do not provide any other text or markdown fences.

Here is the original Java 8 code you have to rewrite:
<original_code>
//package codeforcespractice;
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;
public class vanyaandscale {
static long[] a;
static boolean ans;
static int n;
static long leftsum,rightsum;
public static void main(String[] arg) throws Exception
{
    BufferedReader br=new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));
    StringTokenizer st=new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());
    long w=Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());
    long m=Long.parseLong(st.nextToken());
    long limit=(long)1e11;
    a=new long[40];
    int z=1;
    long temp=1;
    a[0]=1;
    if(w<=3)
    {
        System.out.println("YES");
        System.exit(0);
    }
    for(int i=1;i<16;i++)
    {
        a[z]=temp*w;
        temp=temp*w;
        if(temp>limit)
        {
            break;
        }
        z++;
    }

    leftsum=0;
    rightsum=m;
    n=z;
    pos(0);
    //System.out.println("hello");
    if(ans)
    {
        System.out.println("YES");
    }
    else
    {
        System.out.println("NO");
    }

}
public static void  pos(int x)
{
    if(x==n)
    {
        if(leftsum==rightsum)
        {
            //System.out.println("left sum is special "+leftsum+" rightsum is"+rightsum);
            ans=true;
        }
        return;
    }
    //System.out.println("left sum is"+leftsum+" right sum is"+rightsum);
    if(ans)
    {
        return;
    }
    else
    {
        for(int i=0;i<3;i++)
        {
            if(ans)
            {
                return;
            }
            if(i==1)
            {
                leftsum+=a[x];
                pos(x+1);
                leftsum-=a[x];
            }
            else if(i==2)
            {
                rightsum+=a[x];
                pos(x+1);
                rightsum-=a[x];
            }
            else
            {
                pos(x+1);
            }
        }
    }
}
}

